With a view to making the basic banking facilities available in a more uniform manner across banking system,
RBI has modified the guidelines on opening of basic banking ‘no-frills’ accounts’.Such accounts are now known
as “Basic Savings Bank Deposit” Account which offers the minimum common facilities as under:-
– The account should be considered as a normal banking service available to all;
– No requirement of minimum balance;
– Facilitate deposit and withdrawal of cash at bank branch as well as ATMs;
– Receipt/credit of money through electronic payment channels or by means of cheques/ collection of
cheques drawn by Central/State Government Agencies and departments;
– Account holders are permitted a maximum of four withdrawals in a month including ATM withdrawals;
